# Ghostly Dancers: "return an enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand or unlock a locked door of a Room you control".
# Bot1's Thought Scour mills Bot2's Oblivion Ring on turn 1, and Bot2 casts Grand Entryway on turn 2, its Elegant Rotunda door
# still locked: an enchantment card in an opponent's graveyard and a Room with a locked door an opponent controls. Bot1 has no
# enchantment card in its own graveyard and no Room. On turn 5 Ghostly Dancers enters with neither option possible (CR 608.2d), so
# nothing happens: Oblivion Ring stays in Bot2's graveyard and Bot2's Elegant Rotunda stays locked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Thought Scour
Ghostly Dancers
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Grand Entryway // Elegant Rotunda
Island x4
Oblivion Ring
Island x12

